WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A surface fire exposes one side of a tree stem. Heat enters through the bark on the exposed side.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Heat diffuses inward through bark and wood, and the interior keeps warming after the flames have peaked.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:26.500
Tissue that exceeds 60 degrees Celsius dies. The necrotic depth grows as the thermal wave moves inward.

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Validated heat-transfer models convert a fire's thermal history into tree mortality predictions.
